From f63cd799c897386ff6db4420b0a1cbf8d54153ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 21:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CI shape: when to fold tiny serial jobs into one job
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Owner ruling, 2026-11-13: card "A. Collapse into one job", then "update
skills and processes to see when need to do so". Measured: one content
layer's run took 23 min for about 2.5 min of work, its five small serial
jobs each queuing for a runner (9m29s, 1m, 1m45s, 3m43s, 4m22s).

- ci-health §"A slow workflow can be mostly waiting": when to act (median
  queue wait over run time, or a serial chain of more than 2 jobs each
  under 1 min); how to see it (Actions API job created_at, started_at and
  completed_at, as medians over recent default-branch runs; a tools report
  is to come); what stays separate (heavy or parallel shards, other
  permissions, runners or environments, check names read by merge:guard,
  branch protection or verdict reuse, unless the readers move too); and
  who looks (the weekly CI health review, which opens a work item).
- ci-health-watch.bpmn: the weekly check step measures job shape too;
  .pot files regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPc2tT1vUufdyDbQTBz
